<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply rose $2.1 bln in March 3 wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $2.1 bln in March 3 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $2.1 billion in the March 3 week to $3,871.4 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $6.9 billion to $5,024.5 billion. M-1 fell $0.4 billion to $1,080.2 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,867.8 billion versus $3,865.4 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
